                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.30962/2611.30962v1/CUA-SEE.png",
                "caption": "Figure 3:System overview.\nCUA-SEE forms a closed loop of task evolution, verifier evolution, and agent-environment rollout, as summarized by the central workflow.\nThe left panel details task evolution: rollout evidence is first aggregated at the batch level to plan the next round, followed by two complementary forms of per-task evolution: benchmark evolution for population-level measurement growth and diagnostic evolution for agent-conditional boundary refinement. The right panel presents verifier evolution, which progressively translates evolved task requirements into grounded, executable, and rigorously validated measurements.\nThe bottom panel shows the shared substrate that supports all stages of the evaluation loop, expanding the 8 OSWorld applications to 20 verifiable desktop environments.",
                "position": 481
            }
        ]
